-- title:
--   Principal colorings, path congruences and the algebra of label-decreasing maps
-- statement:
--   Notation follows the base definitions of the graph criterion. Throughout, $L$ is a lattice with least element $\bot$ (several of the facts below need less), $V$ is a set of vertices, and a *coloring* is a map $c:V\times V\to L$. A self-map $p:V\to V$ is *admissible* (label-decreasing) for $c$ if $c(p(x),p(y))\le c(x,y)$ for all $x,y\in V$; collapsing a pair to a single vertex is allowed. For a finite set $S\subseteq V\times V$ of *seed pairs*, a pair $(x,y)$ is *marked* if $x=p(s)$ and $y=p(s')$ for some admissible $p$ and some $(s,s')\in S$, and $\mathrm{Conn}_S$ is the equivalence relation on $V$ generated by the marked pairs. A *graph witness* is a coloring that is symmetric, satisfies $c(x,y)=\bot\iff x=y$ and the triangle inequality $c(x,y)\le c(x,m)\vee c(m,y)$, detects the order of $L$ (whenever $u\not\le v$, some pair has $c(x,y)\le u$ and $c(x,y)\not\le v$), and has the connectivity property: for every nonempty finite $S$, $c(x,y)\le\bigvee_{(s,s')\in S}c(s,s')$ implies $(x,y)\in\mathrm{Conn}_S$. Algebras, congruences, principal congruences $\mathrm{Cg}(a,b)$ and basic translations are as in the congruence file, and $\operatorname{Con}(\mathbf A)$ is ordered by inclusion.
--
--   1. **Principal coloring.** Let $\mathbf A$ be an algebra with carrier $A$ (of any size) and let $\varphi:L\to\operatorname{Con}(\mathbf A)$ be an order isomorphism. The principal coloring of $A$ is
--   $$c_\varphi(a,b)=\varphi^{-1}\bigl(\mathrm{Cg}(a,b)\bigr)\in L\qquad(a,b\in A),$$
--   and it satisfies $c_\varphi(a,b)\le u\iff(a,b)\in\varphi(u)$ for every $u\in L$. Every basic translation of $\mathbf A$ is admissible for $c_\varphi$.
--   2. **Admissible maps act on marked and connected pairs.** For any coloring with values in a preordered set, a composite of admissible maps is admissible; consequently an admissible map $q$ sends every marked pair $(x,y)$ to the marked pair $(q(x),q(y))$, and every $\mathrm{Conn}_S$-related pair to a $\mathrm{Conn}_S$-related pair.
--   3. **Path congruence.** With $\varphi$ as in item 1 and any finite $S\subseteq A\times A$, the relation $\mathrm{Conn}_S$ formed with respect to the principal coloring $c_\varphi$ is a congruence of the original algebra $\mathbf A$, not merely an equivalence relation stable under admissible maps.
--   4. **Graph algebra.** For a finite set $V$ and any coloring $c$, $\mathbf A_c$ is the algebra on $V$ whose basic operations are all admissible self-maps of $V$, each taken once as a unary operation (there are finitely many, listed in an arbitrary fixed order). Every congruence of $\mathbf A_c$ is preserved by every admissible map.
--   5. **Label congruences.** For a finite set $V$, a graph witness $c$ and $u\in L$,
--   $$\theta_u=\{(x,y)\in V\times V:\ c(x,y)\le u\}$$
--   is a congruence of $\mathbf A_c$, and $\theta_u\subseteq\theta_v\iff u\le v$ for all $u,v\in L$.
--   6. **Connectivity stays inside congruences.** For a finite set $V$ and any coloring $c$: if $\theta$ is a congruence of $\mathbf A_c$ and $S$ is a finite set of pairs all of which are related by $\theta$, then $\mathrm{Conn}_S\subseteq\theta$.
--   7. **The isomorphism.** If $V$ is finite and nonempty and $c$ is a graph witness, then every congruence of $\mathbf A_c$ equals $\theta_u$ for some $u\in L$, and
--   $$L\to\operatorname{Con}(\mathbf A_c),\qquad u\mapsto\theta_u,$$
--   is an order isomorphism.
--
--   These are the two halves of the graph characterization of finite congruence lattices. Items 1 to 3 turn a representation $L\cong\operatorname{Con}(\mathbf A)$ into an $L$-colored graph on the carrier of $\mathbf A$, the path congruence being what yields the connectivity property; items 4 to 7 turn a graph witness back into an algebra of unary operations whose congruence lattice is isomorphic to $L$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The definitions are `principalColor` (taking an order isomorphism `equiv : Lat ≃o Congruence alg`), `pathCongruence` (the setoid `Relation.EqvGen.setoid` of `Marked (principalColor equiv) seeds`), `graphAlgebra` (whose `numOps` is the cardinality of the subtype of admissible maps, enumerated with `Fintype.equivFin`, every arity being $1$), `labelCongruence` (which takes the proof of `IsGraphWitness color` as an argument) and `graphOrderIso` (which requires `[Nonempty Carrier]`). The lemmas are `principalColor_le`, `Admissible.comp`, `marked_map`, `connected_map`, `translation_admissible`, `graphAlgebra_preserves`, `labelCongruence_apply`, `labelCongruence_le_iff`, `connected_below_congruence` and `labelCongruence_surjective`. Finiteness of $V$ is the instance `[Fintype Carrier]`; the predicates `Admissible`, `Marked`, `Connected` and `IsGraphWitness` are the base definitions of the challenge statement.
